    "narrative": "For the Zurich Zebras on this May 14th slate, the offensive engine is anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (73.06) and **Kyle Schwarber** (66.74), who provide our highest efficiency ceilings. While **Yordan Alvarez** faces a stern test against Luis Castillo, his elite xwOBA of .421 and favorable platoon advantage in the 3-hole make him an auto-start despite the SP xERA of 4.06. **Kyle Schwarber** earns a premier spot at 66.74; even against an arm like Ranger Suarez, the combination of a positive park factor and a top-of-the-order assignment maximizes his plate appearances, which is critical for our daily Roto volume. **Trea Turner** (64.53) remains a high-priority play; although he faces a tough matchup, his elite sprint speed and historical efficiency against lefties make him the focal point of our stolen base strategy, a category where we remain hyper-aggressive.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Dillon Dingler** (33.06). While his raw projection hovered near our threshold, he was ultimately disqualified due to an unfavorable matchup against a high-skill arm (McLean) and a severe platoon disadvantage. Conversely, we are keeping **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (42.58) in the lineup despite the risk of facing Chris Sale, purely because his defensive utility and potential for stolen bases outweigh the floor-busting risk of the pitcher. We must keep a close watch on the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Caleb Durbin**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Hyeseong Kim**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**; if these players shift lower in the batting order or are pulled for rest, their scores will likely crater, and we will need to pivot to our deeper bench options to preserve our game caps.",
